## Notes

{% if is_typescript %}
The TypeScript sources run **directly** on Node -- there is no compile step.
Node's native type stripping erases the annotations at load time, which is why
`npm start` and `npm test` work on a clean checkout. Type *checking* still
needs `tsc`, wired up via `tsconfig.json` (`erasableSyntaxOnly` keeps the code
within what Node can strip: no enums, no parameter properties).
{% else %}
Plain ESM JavaScript with JSDoc-free, dependency-free code. `node --test`
discovers `test/*.test.js` on its own.
{% endif %}

`greeter.{{ source_ext }}` does no I/O, which keeps the tests fast and lets the
same logic be imported from anywhere.
